2","section":1,"section_title":"Introduction","source":{"current_hash_method":"tex-environment-body-comments-removed","current_statement_sha256":"sha256:67a35e2ea7d84e3eb8c12d0da9c20a59e6239c20416879148672fd2fda8269a4","file":"preprints/Elementary-Positivity-of-Chromatic-Quasisymmetric-Functions-September-24-2026/build/sections/01-introduction.tex","line":39,"producer_hash_method":"atlas-whitespace-normalized-text","producer_statement_sha256":"8b0ba4e23e92d19475e00b1733c8da750664c049aad6fbb5a7faabe095d60298","provenance":{"kind":"computed","pin":"fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb","source":"preprints/Elementary-Positivity-of-Chromatic-Quasisymmetric-Functions-September-24-2026/build/sections/01-introduction.tex"},"sha256":"sha256:67a35e2ea7d84e3eb8c12d0da9c20a59e6239c20416879148672fd2fda8269a4","url":"https://github.com/openai/math/blob/fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb/preprints/Elementary-Positivity-of-Chromatic-Quasisymmetric-Functions-September-24-2026/build/sections/01-introduction.tex#L39"},"statement_kind":"theorem","text":"\\label{main:theorem}\nThere is a deterministic terminating procedure which, given a natural\nunit interval graph $G$ on $[n]$ and $\\sigma\\in D_G^0$, returns a partition\n$\\theta_G(\\sigma)\\vdash n$ such that\n\\begin{equation}\n \\chi_G(X;q)=\\sum_{\\sigma\\in D_G^0}\n       q^{\\ginv_G(\\sigma)}e_{\\theta_G(\\sigma)}(X).\n \\label{main:witness}\n\\end{equation}\nIn particular every elementary coefficient of $\\chi_G(X;q)$ belongs to\n$\\N[q]$. The assertion holds as a formal symmetric-function identity,\nuniformly in $n$ and $G$."}
